"{\"blocks\":[{\"k\":\"t\",\"v\":\"There is no complete award itinerary in these selected results to recommend. The useful next step is to verify the January 9 United lead first: it reports 55,000 United miles and 9 seats, with USD 16.20 in award taxes, but gives no flight schedule. The seat count is reported evidence, not a guarantee of current availability.\"},{\"k\":\"l\",\"r\":\"A26@2027-01-09/SFO>BKK/E\",\"n\":\"United award lead — January 9\",\"v\":\"SFO–BKK in economy; 55,000 United miles and USD 16.20 in award taxes. The result reports 9 seats, but only a date—not departure or arrival times, flights, or connections—so it is not a bookable itinerary as shown. Its lower reported fee than the other selected award lead may be useful, but it requires 12,500 more program miles.\"},{\"k\":\"l\",\"r\":\"A3@2027-01-01/SFO>BKK/E\",\"n\":\"Alaska award lead — January 1\",\"v\":\"SFO–BKK in economy; 42,500 Alaska miles and USD 50.90 in award taxes. It reports 8 seats but no schedule, flights, or connections. Its lower points requirement may appeal if you have Alaska miles, but the higher reported fee and January 1 date are tradeoffs; this is also not a complete itinerary as shown.\"},{\"k\":\"b\",\"r\":\"C1@2027-01-01T22:55-08:00/SFO>BKK\",\"n\":\"Cash benchmark — Cathay Pacific, January 1\",\"v\":\"A timed one-stop SFO–HKG–BKK itinerary, departing 10:55 p.m. January 1 and arriving 10:35 a.m. January 4 local time; elapsed time is 44 hours 40 minutes. The quoted cash fare is USD 640.00, but its price scope is unknown, so it cannot be treated as a per-person or all-in total. This is a cash comparison, not an award itinerary.\"},{\"k\":\"t\",\"v\":\"The two award leads are dated January 1 and January 9, but neither provides a schedule, so their travel times and connections cannot be compared. The award cabin is reported as economy; individual leg cabins are not specified. Search coverage was partial, and no complete selectable journey was found in the results represented here. Confirm current award availability and fees with the program before relying on either lead.\"}]}"
